# Commits that only reformatted code. `git blame` skips them and attributes each
# line to the change before, so a mass reformat does not hide who wrote what.
#
# Use it locally once per clone:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
# GitHub's blame view reads this file automatically.
#
# List the commit as it exists ON MAIN. Pull requests land as squash merges, so
# the SHAs of commits inside a PR branch never reach main - record the squash
# commit's SHA, after the merge, in a follow-up commit. One full 40-character SHA
# per line, with a comment saying what it was.
#
# Prettier across backend/, web/ and site/ (#310, #471). The squash also carries
# the CI format check and the pre-commit hook, which add lines rather than
# reformat them, so ignoring the whole commit costs no real attribution.
